#
# ── How prove_loop works ──
#
# `bb-avm prove_loop` is a long-running daemon that:
#   - Keeps SRS mmap, thread pool, and proving key cache alive between proofs
#   - Reads JSON-line requests from stdin, writes JSON-line responses to stdout
#   - Supports warmup via --warmup-dir or per-request {"type":"warmup"} messages
#   - Supports per-request concurrency override via {"concurrency": N}
#   - Graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT
#
# Expected savings: ~800ms/proof from avoiding:
#   - SRS mmap reload (~200-300ms)
#   - Thread pool initialization (~100-200ms)
#   - Proving key cache cold-start (~200-500ms)
#
# ── Architecture notes ──
#
# - 3 prover agents = 3 separate Node.js processes, each gets its own daemon(s)
# - Within one Node.js process, daemons are keyed by flavor string
# - Most proofs use ultra_rollup_honk (BaseRollup, merges, block root)
# - Parity uses ultra_honk, RootRollup uses ultra_keccak_honk
# - The daemon protocol is serial per flavor (one request at a time per daemon)
#
# ── To revert ──
# Reinstall aztec packages: cd ~/.aztec/versions/4.1.3 && npm install
# Or restore original binary from npm cache (~/.npm/_cacache backup).
